From d800dec3ca9159eadffaaec4e7b213324e9952b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rustcc-build <rustcc@localhost>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 02:30:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] P09.x (1.13.6 RA parity): transparent base-member resolution
 for `class`
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The fork rustc gives a derived `class D : B` transparent base-member
access by synthesizing `impl Deref for D { type Target = B; ... }`. RA
models `class` natively (no synthetic impl), so this teaches RA's
field resolution + completion to walk the `#[rustc_cxx_base]` base
chain directly, matching the compiler.

- `hir_ty::lower::class_base_ty` (new, re-exported): lowers a class's
  base type ref in its generic context, returning `EarlyBinder<Ty>`.
  Instantiated with the derived class's args, it yields the concrete
  base type — so multi-level chains and generic bases substitute
  correctly.
- Field resolution (`InferenceContext::lookup_field`, ClassId arm) now
  walks the base chain via `resolve_class_field_chain`: if a field
  isn't declared directly on the class, recurse into the base type and
  resolve there, returning the base `FieldId` with the base's subst.
  A field declared on the derived class wins over a same-named base
  field (C++ name-hiding), since the derived class is checked first.
- `hir::Type::fields` appends base-class fields (deduped by name) so
  base fields show up in dot-completion. Method resolution + method
  completion already walked the base (`base_class_of` in the probe),
  so `self.base_method()` was already fine.

Tests: `class_inherited_field_access`, `class_multilevel_field_access`,
`class_generic_base_field_access`, `class_derived_shadows_base_field`
(hir-ty inference); `completes_inherited_class_fields_via_dot`
(ide-completion). hir-ty (976) + ide-completion (730) suites green.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
